.nh
.TH "PVEFORGE" "1" "Sep 2026" "pveforge" "pveforge manual"

.SH NAME
pveforge-storage-alloc - Allocate a convention-named raw volume, idempotently


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpveforge storage alloc <target-id> <storage> <filename> <size> <vmid> [--format F] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Allocate a raw volume on a storage by a caller-chosen, deterministic
filename (POST /nodes/{node}/storage/{storage}/content), idempotently — the
"pvesm alloc" half of raw-volume lifecycle, for volumes outside qm's own disk
schema.

.PP
The filename is the identity: absent -> allocated; already present with that
name for that vmid -> no-op (nothing changed). The allocate call is synchronous
(no task wait); success is confirmed by a dual signal — the volid the POST
returned is read back from the storage listing.

.PP
size is PVE's own size grammar (e.g. 32G), passed through unchanged. --format is
optional (PVE infers it from the storage type when omitted).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--force\fP[=false]
	re-run Apply even if the volume already exists (PVE then refuses the duplicate)

.PP
\fB--format\fP=""
	the volume format (raw, qcow2, ...); optional, PVE infers from the storage type when omitted

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for alloc

.PP
\fB--lock-wait\fP=0s
	how long to wait for another pveforge process's lock on this object before giving up (0 = the 15m0s default; at most 1h0m0s). The default exceeds the 10m0s ceiling on waiting for a PVE task because a legitimate lock holder may be in such a wait the whole time

.PP
\fB--roster\fP=""
	path to the roster file (overrides PVEFORGE_ROSTER and the default ./pveforge.toml)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpveforge-storage(1)\fP
